Bibleit Lua SDK notices

Bibleit-authored code, the wire contract and shared protocol fixtures are licensed
under the repository MIT license. The Lua protocol/domain implementation adapts
behavior from Bibleit Go (https://github.com/bibleit-labs/bibleit-go), retaining
its MIT attribution in LICENSE and docs/LICENSE.

Lua operation/schema metadata follows the checked-in public OpenAPI contract. Go code-generator templates and Go
runtime dependencies are not included in this package.

Runtime dependencies are installed separately by LuaRocks:

- dkjson: MIT/X11, https://dkolf.de/dkjson-lua/
- LuaSocket: MIT, https://github.com/lunarmodules/luasocket
- LuaSec: MIT, https://github.com/lunarmodules/luasec
- OpenSSL (used by LuaSec): https://www.openssl.org/source/license.html

Retain each dependency's own license/notices when redistributing its source or
native binaries. This package's .all.rock contains Lua modules and documentation;
it does not bundle native dependency binaries.

The optional development formatter is LuaLS/EmmyLuaCodeStyle, invoked through
sumneko.lua. It is not part of the runtime package.

Development tests use LuaUnit (BSD), https://github.com/bluebird75/luaunit.
It is installed separately and is not a runtime dependency.
